From 0b46cb9411ceb4c731c4584051714fc4077ac4e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:51:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Amiga: stop on Ctrl-C while compressing, without a
 partial archive

On UNIX, SIGINT runs interrupt(), which removes the temporary archive.
AROS's C library raises no SIGINT while a program reads files, so Ctrl-C
had no effect until lha ended, and a program running lha could not stop
it. The Ctrl-C signal is now checked before each block is read; when it
is set, the same cleanup() removes the temporary file and lha ends with
return code 20.

Repository: lha (https://github.com/sodero/lha.git)
Base: 1e7c8f1fc1bd0f72610ca381e21bbda9325cd4f5
Requires: 0001-Amiga-no-UNIX-permission-headers-beside-the-protecti.patch, 0002-Amiga-no-trailing-NUL-in-the-name-when-there-is-no-c.patch, 0003-Add-list-FILE-archive-and-file-names-from-a-file.patch
Scope: Amiga builds (_AMIGA)
Tested: AROS One 1.3, ABIv11 x86_64 (2026-10-18): a 1229-entry Amiga tree packed and read back identically by Unarc (XAD), and by C:lha except comments, which it does not set; Amiga LhA 2.15, LHa for UNIX and 7-Zip test it OK
Upstream-Status: candidate (not submitted)
Removal: when sodero/lha carries an equivalent change and the pin moves past it
---
 src/crcio.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/crcio.c b/src/crcio.c
index e96a723..b181927 100644
--- a/src/crcio.c
+++ b/src/crcio.c
@@ -7,6 +7,10 @@
 /*  Ver. 1.14   Source All chagned              1995.01.14  N.Watazaki      */
 /* ------------------------------------------------------------------------ */
 #include "lha.h"
+#if _AMIGA
+#include <proto/exec.h>
+#include <dos/dos.h>
+#endif
 
 /* ------------------------------------------------------------------------ */
 #ifdef EUC
@@ -51,6 +55,16 @@ fread_crc(crcp, p, n, fp)
     int  n;
     FILE *fp;
 {
+#if _AMIGA
+    /* Ctrl-C: stop between blocks and remove the unfinished archive. The C
+       library raises no SIGINT while reading a file, so the signal handler
+       that does this on UNIX never runs here. */
+    if (SetSignal(0, SIGBREAKF_CTRL_C) & SIGBREAKF_CTRL_C) {
+        message("Interrupted");
+        cleanup();
+        exit(20);
+    }
+#endif
     if (text_mode)
         n = fread_txt(p, n, fp);
     else
